Subject: Cantor Seeded Compiler Slice 6 Native Build Receipt Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 43105752-8efa-4911-8b45-1a278ec2509f
@ [source_uuid] a22089f8-8790-4b8d-9951-11bd9752be59
@ [review_uuid] ab6e1f84-6fcc-427f-9467-1175909f833c

& [Problem]
  + Slice5 can identify a reproducible native build candidate but cannot report that bytes were built
  + treating candidate metadata or its read-only plan receipt as build permission would violate backend and authority boundaries

& [Decision]
  + add a later-stage native execution plan capability receipt sandbox admission dual approval build observation artifact receipt and independent verification lifecycle
  + implement only pure validation projection replay signature verification and supplied-runner boundaries in cantor_core
  + leave the production physical process runner inactive until its target sandbox has independent evidence

& [Why]
  + exact later-stage forms make process authority inspectable without granting it to semantic compilation
  + dual approval connects Security containment and external authority while keeping keys outside model control
  + supplied observations let an effectful host report results without importing ambient I/O into deterministic core semantics
  + produced_unverified prevents successful exit or a digest from masquerading as correctness

& [Rejected]
  + reuse Slice5 CandidateCompilationPlan capability receipt because its request is intentionally read-only
  + call std::process::Command directly from the semantic projector because that hides ambient host and sandbox authority
  + call Cargo success an ArtifactVerificationReceipt because build success is only an observation
  + claim reproducibility from one build because equality requires at least two independently identified observations

& [Support]
  + source preservation SJS review requirement matrix phase lock adversarial tests and complete workspace verification support the pure lifecycle seam
  + physical runner support remains explicitly absent and cannot be inferred from this implementation
